  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "When Chef Barinov, Senya, and Lyova open the cooler, they think the inspector has crawled into the ventilation shaft. After sending Lyova up into the narrow duct, they realize the inspector was hiding behind stacked boxes all along.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Он ушёл прямо по вентиляции.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Кто теперь полезет за ним?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я на повороте могу застрять.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Подождите, как я его узнаю?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Там нет других людей внутри.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы пока изучим план вентиляции.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Лёва, ты там в порядке?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Он обязательно доползёт до конца.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Держи фрукты и овощи отдельно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я так и сделал вчера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Кто эти коробки туда сгрузил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Смотри, он всё ещё там!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Он ушёл прямо по вентиляции.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He left right through the ventilation shaft.' Notice how Russian expresses 'he' and 'ventilation shaft' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Кто теперь полезет за ним?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Who is going to climb in after him now?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'who' before landing on 'him'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я на повороте могу застрять.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I might get stuck at the turn.' In Russian, the idea of 'I' flows naturally into 'to get stuck' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Подождите, как я его узнаю?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait, how will I recognize him?' Lyova raises the pitch on 'will find out' to turn the phrase into a direct spoken question. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Там нет других людей внутри.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There are no other people inside there.' Notice how Russian expresses 'there' and 'inside' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы пока изучим план вентиляции.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Meanwhile we will study the ventilation plan.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'we' before landing on 'ventilation shaft'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Лёва, ты там в порядке?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Lyova, are you alright in there?' In Russian, the idea of 'Lyova' flows naturally into 'order' without extra filler words. Senya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Он обязательно доползёт до конца.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He will definitely crawl to the end.' Senya anchors the line on 'he', while 'end' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Держи фрукты и овощи отдельно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Keep the fruits and vegetables separate.' The grammar packs 'hold' and 'separately' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я так и сделал вчера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I did just that yesterday.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'yesterday' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Кто эти коробки туда сгрузил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Who unloaded those boxes over there?' In Russian, the idea of 'who' flows naturally into 'unloaded' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Смотри, он всё ещё там!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Look, he is still right there!' The meaning hinges on 'watch' working together with 'there' in spoken Russian. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
